title: Rifles and Ammunition
subtitle: The fighting groups are short of everything.
view-if: crisis_march = 1
on-arrival: month_actions += 1
frequency: 100
is-card: true
new-page: true
tags: crisis

= Rifles and Ammunition

The fighting groups in the Mansfeld villages have shotguns, a few army rifles from 1918 and almost no ammunition. The miners have dynamite. The police have machine guns and armoured cars.

- @depots: Raid the police and Reichswehr depots.
- @miners: Arm the Mansfeld miners with what we have.
- @bury: Bury the rifles for another day.

@depots
subtitle: [? if lock_uprising = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] The Left's line. Arms for the fight, and a reason for the state to hit back harder.
choose-if: lock_uprising < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids armed action.
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.lock_uprising == 1) {
    Q.unity -= 10;
    Q[Q.leading_faction + '_satisfaction'] -= 10;
}
Q.red_guards_arms += 10;
Q.crisis_momentum += 5;
Q.repression += 6;
Q.offensive_satisfaction += 3;
Q.lean_offensive += 2;
!}

A night raid on a police barracks near Eisleben brings in two hundred rifles and a machine gun. Two of our men are killed.

@miners
subtitle: More men under arms. Better if we already have arms to give them.
on-arrival: {!
Q.crisis_momentum += (Q.red_guards_arms >= 20) ? 6 : 2;
Q.red_guards_strength += 3;
Q.repression += 3;
Q.lean_offensive += 1;
!}

The miners' fighting groups double in size in a day. Half of the new men have nothing but a pick handle.

@bury
subtitle: The Right's caution: keep the arms for a fight we can win.
on-arrival: e21_arms_saved = 1; crisis_momentum -= 3; red_guards_arms += 3; unionist_satisfaction += 3; luxemburgist_satisfaction += 2; lean_unionist += 1

The rifles are greased, wrapped in oilcloth and buried in the allotments. The men who bury them are told to forget where.
